trivy fs  Vulnerabilities  scaanning  --scanners misconfig
      Misconfigurations(--image-config-scanners misconfig,--image-config-scanners secret)

     aftrer te build 

          trivy image
          trivy config ./iac-directory
          trivy fs --scanners vuln,misconfig,secret ./myapp


A. Vulnerability Database Cache (DB Cache)
B. Scan Analysis Cache (Scan Cache)

Advanced: Unified vs. Raw Scanning (--raw-config-scanners)


rivy’s Cryptographic Asset Scanning (--scanners crypto) automatically audits digital certificates, cryptographic keys, and encryption algorithms inside a container image. It generates a Cryptography Bill of Materials (CBOM) embedded within a CycloneDX JSON report.

2. Host the Database Internally

Because security databases update daily, pre-baking trivy-db into the runner image will make your security scans stale over time. Instead:

    Set up a daily cron job on an internet-connected machine to pull ghcr.io/aquasecurity/trivy-db:2 and mirror it to your internal container registry (e.g., Harbor, JFrog Artifactory, or AWS ECR).

    Point your Trivy pipeline step to your internal mirror:

YAML

      - name: Run Trivy Scan (Internal DB Mirror)
        run: |
          trivy image \
            --db-repository internal-registry.company.com/aquasecurity/trivy-db \
            --severity HIGH,CRITICAL \
            --exit-code 1 \
            my-app:latest


